  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Suppose $(8a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $b\\cdot a=4(a\\cdot a)$\n\nII. $-a\\cdot a<0$\n\nIII. $b\\cdot a=4$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Simplifying the expression $(8a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (8a)\\cdot a+(2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 8(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 2(b\\cdot a) & =-8(a\\cdot a) \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-4(a\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0$, which implies $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\n- Statement III is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 8(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 8(a\\cdot a)+2(4) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
